The menstrual cycle runs through four phases in this order:
- **Menstrual phase** (days 3 to 5), when the endometrial lining breaks down and menstrual flow occurs;
- **Follicular (proliferative) phase**, when the primary follicles grow into a Graafian follicle and the endometrium regenerates;
- **Ovulatory phase**, around the middle of the cycle (about day 14), when the LH surge ruptures the Graafian follicle and the ovum is released;
- **Luteal (secretory) phase**, when the remaining parts of the Graafian follicle form the corpus luteum, which secretes progesterone.

So the answer is option (C) Menstrual phase, Follicular phase, Ovulatory phase, Luteal phase.
